This error means Spring cannot see your AsciiPathConfig class. This usually happens if the class is missing the @Configuration annotation or is in a folder Spring isn't scanning.
Let's fix the error and move the logic to a separate file as you asked. This is a much cleaner "Professional" structure.
1. Fix the Config Class (AsciiPathConfig.java)
Crucial: You must add @Configuration at the top, or Spring will never find it.
package com.tcs.fincore.AsciiGenerationService.Config;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration; // <--- MUST HAVE THIS

@Configuration  // <--- IF YOU MISS THIS, YOU GET THE "BEAN NOT FOUND" ERROR
public class AsciiPathConfig {

    @Value("${source.file.path}")
    private String sourceFilePath;

    public String getSourceFilePath() {
        return sourceFilePath;
    }
}

2. Create the Separate Test Runner (AsciiTestRunner.java)
Create this new file inside com.tcs.fincore.AsciiGenerationService. This file will handle the "Test Logic" (reading and printing) so your Main file stays clean.
package com.tcs.fincore.AsciiGenerationService;

import com.tcs.fincore.AsciiGenerationService.Config.AsciiPathConfig;
import org.springframework.boot.CommandLineRunner;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component; // <--- IMPORTANT

import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Paths;
import java.util.List;

@Component // <--- This tells Spring: "Run this class automatically"
public class AsciiTestRunner implements CommandLineRunner {

    private final AsciiPathConfig asciiConfig;

    // Constructor Injection (Better than @Autowired)
    public AsciiTestRunner(AsciiPathConfig asciiConfig) {
        this.asciiConfig = asciiConfig;
    }

    @Override
    public void run(String... args) {
        System.out.println(">>> TEST RUNNER STARTED <<<");

        try {
            String path = asciiConfig.getSourceFilePath();
            System.out.println("Target Path: " + path);

            if (path == null) {
                System.err.println("❌ Path is NULL. Check application.properties!");
                return;
            }

            // Read and Print
            List<String> lines = Files.readAllLines(Paths.get(path));
            System.out.println("--- FILE CONTENT ---");
            lines.forEach(System.out::println);
            System.out.println("--------------------");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("❌ Error Reading File: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}

3. Clean the Main File (AsciiGenerationServiceApplication.java)
Now we remove all the logic from here. It just starts the app.
package com.tcs.fincore.AsciiGenerationService;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;

@SpringBootApplication
public class AsciiGenerationServiceApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(AsciiGenerationServiceApplication.class, args);
    }
    
    // No logic here! The AsciiTestRunner will run automatically.
}

Summary of Fixes
 * Added @Configuration to AsciiPathConfig (Fixes "Bean not found").
 * Created AsciiTestRunner with @Component (Moves logic to separate file).
 * Cleaned Main (Keeps entry point simple).
Run the main file now. Spring will start, find the TestRunner, and execute your file reading logic automatically.
